# amem local memory

amem injects matching local memory into Cursor automatically (session start + each prompt). Treat that packet as the first map of this repo.

1. Prefer amem file anchors over broad greps and multi-folder reads.
2. Still verify current code before editing — memory can be stale.
3. After durable learnings, the stop hook stores a compact session claim. You can also run `amem-update-working-memory` for higher-quality facts.

Do not re-run `amem context` unless the injected packet is empty or clearly wrong.

Memory is personal and stored under `~/.amem` on this machine. Do not commit exports or database copies to shared remotes.

Open the local UI anytime with `amem ui` (setup wizard, brain map, token estimates).
